SUMMARY:PyLadies × R-Ladies Vancouver Lightning Talks - R-Ladies Vancouver
DESCRIPTION:​**PyLadies Vancouver** and **R-Ladies Vancouver** are teaming up for a night of lightning talks: short talks from speakers in both communities. Come for a fast, friendly mix of Python and R, ideas, tools, and stories, all in bite-sized form.\n\nPlease sign up on Luma so we know to expect you: https://luma.com/3gsm7kqq\n\n## ​📢 We're looking for speakers!\n\n​We're looking for short presentations, **5 to 15 minutes long**, from speakers in either community, PyLadies or R-Ladies.\n​• **Beginners especially encouraged.** A lightning talk is a great first talk, and great practice before a conference.\n​• **Never done public speaking?** We'd love to debut you and help launch your speaking journey.\n​• **Yes, you can reuse a talk you've given elsewhere.** New members may not have heard it.\n​• **Python or R**, plus adjacent technology topics. When we polled our last meetup, people asked for: AI/ML and LLMs, web development, data science,Python internals, testing and tooling, and live coding.\n​• **Not sure your topic is interesting enough?** Let us be the judge, sign up with your idea.\n​New to the format? [Our lightning guide](https://vancouver.pyladies.com/lightning-talks/?utm_source=luma) covers what a lightning talk is, how to prepare, topic ideas, example talks to watch, and common questions.\n​[Sign up](https://sessionize.com/pyladies-vancouver-meetup/?utm_source=luma) to give a lightning talk.\n\n​**Free to attend.** We're run entirely by volunteers, so donations are always appreciated and help keep our meetups free and welcoming: [https://psfmember.org/civicrm/contribute/transact/?reset=1&id=60](https://psfmember.org/civicrm/contribute/transact/?reset=1&id=60&utm_source=luma)\n​\n**Everyone is welcome.** This is a joint event with R-Ladies Vancouver.\n​PyLadies events follow the [PyLadies Code of Conduct](https://www.pyladies.com/CodeOfConduct/?utm_source=luma).\n​If it's your first R-Ladies event, please review the[ R-Ladies Global Code of Conduct](https://www.pyladies.com/CodeOfConduct/?utm_source=luma).\n​Both communities share a focus on supporting women and gender-diverse people in ourfield.
LOCATION:See Luma page, 11111, Vancouver, CANADA
URL:https://www.meetup.com/rladies-vancouver/events/315798255/
ORGANIZER;CN=R-Ladies Vancouver:mailto:info@rladies.org
CATEGORIES:RLadies+,R-Ladies Vancouver
